# Upstream shipped this as a whitelist: `*` then one `!` per test file. Any test added afterwards
# is silently ignored -- five files and ~40 tests written on 2026-08-06 were invisible to `git
# add -A` and would have been lost. Whitelist the PATTERN instead of individual files.
# `*` still catches __pycache__, .pyc and any dataset/output dropped in here.
*
!dataset
!.gitignore
!*_test.py
